# ____title____
#
# A document that is read aloud. `pnpm build` says this and films index.html
# scrolling to wherever the voice is. `pnpm pdf` prints the same page.
#
#   [slide what]           go to the section the page calls `what`
#   [slide what step:2]    light up the part of it marked data-step="2"
#
# The voice need not read every word on the page. Say what a reader would
# want to be told; the page holds the rest.
#
@characters
NARRATOR: { persona: narrator, name: ____fullName____, title: ____role____ }
---
[speakers lower-third captions]
[slide title]
NARRATOR: This is a short report on how the harbour log is kept.
[speakers captions]
[slide why]
NARRATOR: The log exists for one reason. When a boat is late, somebody has to know when she was last seen.
[slide what]
NARRATOR: So every night, three things are written down.
[slide what step:1]
NARRATOR: When the lamp was lit, to the minute.
[slide what step:2]
NARRATOR: Which boats came in, by name.
[slide what step:3]
NARRATOR: And what the weather did.
[slide rules]
NARRATOR: There are only two rules.
[slide rules step:1]
NARRATOR: Write it the same night.
[slide rules step:2]
NARRATOR: And never rub anything out.
[pause 0.4]
[slide close]
NARRATOR: That is the whole report. The page has the detail.
